 }
+
+// REWINDBOX_ZCLIP_WINDOW_Z_616: Black Ops II draws an object in front of the
+// whole scene with the clip range [1, 1e19] and a viewport Z scale of 1e19
+// over an offset of 1 (window Z = 1 + 1e19 * z_ndc), reversed depth GEQUAL.
+// The RSX capture of BLES01717 attached to RPCS3 issue #13227 (RRC v5,
+// 4,023 draws) holds 26 such draws: a 12-draw depth prepass right after the
+// depth clear, before the 1,544-draw scene prepass, the same 12 draws in the
+// colour pass (GEQUAL against that prepass) and 2 blended draws without
+// depth write. Without float64 nor an unrestricted depth range (MoltenVK),
+// the vertex fallback compresses Z above 1 into [0.99, 1] from clip-space Z
+// (pos.z), not window Z: pos.z - 1 over 1e19 - 1 is the clip-space z_clip,
+// constant (the near distance) for a reversed infinite projection, so every
+// fragment of these draws gets the same depth. The colour pass then keeps the
+// last triangle drawn on a pixel instead of the nearest one: back parts of
+// the forearm and weapon show through the front ones. Compressing the window
+// Z ((d - 1) / (1e19 - 1) = z_ndc) keeps their depth order inside the band.
+// The vertex shader text of this title changes once, so its vertex Metal
+// libraries are compiled again on the next boot.
+constexpr bool requires_zclip_fallback_window_z(std::string_view title_id) noexcept
+{
+	return is_black_ops_ii_title(title_id);
+}
+
+// REWINDBOX_SPU_OBJECT_PREFETCH_616 (ios/IOSSpuObjectPrefetch.h): Black Ops II
+// opens 7,162 cached SPU objects in the first 5 s of a multiplayer match on the
+// Build 614 logs (4.3 s of file reads on the compile threads, a 2.0 s frame).
+constexpr bool requires_spu_object_prefetch(std::string_view title_id) noexcept
+{
+	return is_black_ops_ii_title(title_id);
+}
 }
